## 2026-02-22 - Ripple Heightfield Bring-up Limitations (Jai -> IR -> SPIR-V -> Metal)

### Limitations hit while implementing `src/apps/ripple_heightfield.jai`
- [x] `SPIR-V backend rejected subscripting when the base pointer came from a cast expression in graphics shaders`
  Symptom during bring-up: shader pair transpilation failed with `SPIR-V backend: unknown subscript base '*float2(state)'` when indexing data via a casted pointer derived from `*[N]Vector2`.
  Workaround used: changed graphics shader parameter types to `*Vector2` and indexed directly, removing the casted-pointer subscript pattern.
  Follow-up: support subscripting from cast-derived pointer bases in SPIR-V backend/lowering so `*[N]T` -> `*T` cast + index works consistently across shader stages.
